[IMP] payment, *: queue payment data for serialized processing

*: payment provider modules (`payment_*`), `account_payment`,
   `pos_online_payment_self_order`, `website_payment`, `website_sale`

Before this commit, payment data processing occurred directly within the
payment flow and could be triggered from many different entry points.
This was a structural problem that led to race conditions when multiple
workers attempted to update the same `payment.transaction` record
simultaneously. Indeed, when an HTTP handler receives payment data from
a payment provider and updates the transaction accordingly, a concurrent
write (from a webhook, cron, capture action, etc.) can trigger a
rollback-and-replay. On replay, a non-idempotent API call might be
triggered again, leading to customers being charged twice while Odoo
records only one transaction.

To eliminate the problem entirely, this commit introduces a deferred
processing model: payment data is no longer processed immediately upon
receipt. Instead, raw payloads are queued as records of the
`payment.data` model, and a dedicated cron processes all pending records
serially. Write-write conflicts can no longer happen as only the cron is
allowed to update `payment.transaction` records. This constraint is
enforced by a write guard that raises an error on any direct write
unless the caller explicitly opts in by passing the `payment_safe_write=True` context key.

If processing fails, `payment.data` records are flagged and excluded
from further cron runs, as it is highly unlikely that a second attempt
would succeed before the underlying bug is fixed. A "Mark as Confirmed"
server action is added to transactions to provide a manual workaround.

The UX is preserved by having the client request an immediate execution
of the cron upon reaching the `/payment/status` page, which ensures that
customers receive feedback from their payment as soon as possible,
without waiting for the next scheduled cron run.

